apple-app-store.mdx — after “Existing Bitrise upload”
After processing completes, open TestFlight and confirm the exact version/build. Confirm the intended tester group has access, then have an eligible tester install and verify that build. TestFlight availability does not mean the app is publicly released.

google-play.mdx — under “Existing Bitrise deployment”
Before automated deployment, the authorized owner confirms the required initial console upload, protected service-account binding, application ID, and target track. After deployment, verify the exact version code and intended tester access.

signing-and-release-approval.mdx — under signing setup
Platform Engineering owns protected signing stores and workflow credential bindings. Developers provide application details and inspect results with the owner. Do not create replacement signing credentials to resolve a failed build.

enterprise-app-store.mdx — before installation verification
Check upload, destination signing/policy processing, version enablement, and audience assignment separately. Then verify that an intended user can see the exact version. A successful Bitrise build alone does not confirm distribution.
